  "question": {
    "text": "A conducting soap bubble having a radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo></math> thickness <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mfenced><mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is charged to a potential <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi></math>. If now, the bubble collapses and forms a droplet, then the &nbsp;potential of the droplet is"
  },
